# PX4 is cloned inside the Dockerfile at a pinned SHA, not sent through the
# build context. Excluding it here drops the context from ~412MB / 49,000 files
# to ~10MB, which on macOS is the difference between a 23-minute build and a
# fast one (BuildKit hashes the whole context on EVERY build, cached or not).
#
# The drone parts that live only in px4/Tools/simulation/gz/models
# (x500, x500_base, optical_flow, LW20) still reach the image -- they arrive
# via the clone, not via COPY.
px4/

webapp/frontend/node_modules/
# The UI is built inside the image (stage `webbuild`), so a local build/ is
# dead weight in the context and could only cause confusion about which bundle
# actually shipped.
webapp/frontend/build/
output/
webapp/output/
.venv/
venv/
.git/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Local scratch
docs/superpowers/
